8:Loop keeps playback going round, so you can watch a passage over and over while you adjust it.
10:<AtAGlance where="The Loop button in the toolbar" />
12:## Turn Loop on
14:Click **Loop**, the repeat button at the end of the transport in the toolbar. The button is dimmed while Loop is off and full strength while it's on. Click it again to turn Loop off.
16:Loop has no menu item and no key. It's off when a window opens, it's set for each window on its own, and it isn't saved with the project.
20:| What's set | What Loop repeats |
27:The loop follows as things change. Set a new in or out point, clear the range or change the timeline's length while Loop is on, and the next pass uses the new span.
31:When playback reaches the end of the loop, it jumps back to the loop's start and carries on, at 2× and 4× as well.
33:- Press play at or past the end of the loop and it starts again from the loop's start.

